.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_parens_nest_limit \- get the parentheses nesting limit
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_get_parens_nest_limit\fP\f(CR(pcre2_compile_context *\fP\f(CIccontext\fP\f(CR,
                                uint32_t *\fP\f(CIlimit\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function gets, from a compile context, the maximum depth of nested
parentheses in a pattern. The result is zero. Both arguments must be
non\-\f(CBNULL\fP.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.